{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3088","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3088","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3088\",\"parent_revision\":\"e606f2dfba50ed8ab47e9a57a8a962a7c77aba7bee86796ab62baec298734834\",\"root_revision\":\"e606f2dfba50ed8ab47e9a57a8a962a7c77aba7bee86796ab62baec298734834\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`'s \\\"Plan and artifact capability boundary\\\" section states: \\\"The configured backend implements the logical plan and artifact capabilities. `sam_plan`, `sam_task`, `sam_active_task`, and `artifact_*` calls use that same backend; there is no `TASKBACKEND`, independent artifact provider, local filesystem fallback, or per-plan backend selection.\\\"\\n\\nVerified directly against source: `dh_core/protocols.py` defines a class literally named `TaskBackend`, and `dh_core/operations.py` (which `sam_schema/server.py` imports as `from dh_core import operations`) uses it for plan/task CRUD (`create_plan(backend: TaskBackend, ...)`, `read_plan(backend: TaskBackend, ...)`, `list_plans(backend: TaskBackend, ...)`) \u2014 separate from `WorkItemBackend` (`backlog_core/backend_types.py`), which backlog items (`backlog_add`, `backlog_view`, etc.) use.\\n\\n`dh_core/operations.py`'s own module docstring says it uses \\\"backend protocol (dh_core.protocols) for data access\\\" and its function docstrings describe \\\"Both frontends resolve the configured backend and pass it here\\\" (referring to `TaskBackend` implementations like `GistTaskLayer`, `LocalYamlTaskProvider`) \u2014 this reads as an intentional, documented-in-code design, not an accidental leftover.\\n\\nSeparately, `dh_core/operations.py` also imports `ContentProvider` from `backlog_core.backend_types` \u2014 so artifact retrieval specifically may still route through the same `ContentProvider` protocol backlog items use, while plan/task storage does not. The exact current relationship between `TaskBackend`, `WorkItemBackend`, and `ContentProvider` needs to be established and then AGENTS.md corrected to match, rather than continuing to state a \\\"single shared backend\\\" claim the code doesn't support.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] The actual current relationship between `TaskBackend`, `WorkItemBackend`, and `ContentProvider` is documented accurately (which subsystems use which, and whether any of them share a configured instance)\\n- [ ] AGENTS.md's \\\"Plan and artifact capability boundary\\\" section is corrected to match verified current behavior, not aspirational or stale claims\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer reading the documentation**, I want to **agents.md claims no taskbackend/independent artifact provider exists \u2014 dh_core.protocols.taskbackend contradicts this** so that **documentation is accurate and trustworthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"804c743f9a7c4c3bada802a712ec997d83a77fe83a13bcb2e1e060cb41afc908\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP844tw\"}"}